# KratosOS: never install a mail transfer agent.
#
# A privacy/anti-forensics desktop has no use for a mail server, and MTAs ship
# SUID/SGID binaries (Debian's default exim4 is SUID root with a long history
# of root CVEs; ssmtp is SGID mail). The only path in is a SOFT dependency:
# rkhunter Recommends bsd-mailx, and bsd-mailx hard-depends on ANY MTA, so
# blocking exim4 alone made apt pick ssmtp instead (CI run #242). So block the
# mailx clients that drag an MTA in AND every MTA provider; the Recommends are
# then simply left unsatisfied. Placed in includes.chroot_before_packages so it
# applies while the image is built AND stays in the installed system (an `apt
# install` that hard-requires an MTA now refuses instead of silently adding
# one; remove this file if you genuinely need local mail).
Package: exim4*
Pin: release *
Pin-Priority: -1

Package: postfix*
Pin: release *
Pin-Priority: -1

Package: sendmail*
Pin: release *
Pin-Priority: -1

Package: ssmtp nullmailer dma msmtp-mta opensmtpd courier-mta citadel-mta esmtp-run masqmail
Pin: release *
Pin-Priority: -1

Package: bsd-mailx s-nail mailutils
Pin: release *
Pin-Priority: -1
